// This file is the other half of the siblingalias fixture, and is never
// instrumented: it holds no candidate and comes back byte for byte. It exists
// to bind two names in the package block, which the file beside it must not
// import the generated runtime under. A package-level declaration is not
// shadowed by a file-scoped import alias the way a local variable is — Go
// rejects the redeclaration outright — so an alias chosen by looking at one
// file alone would compile everywhere except here.
package sample

// __gm collides with the alias the instrumenter reaches for first.
var __gm = "taken"

// __gm1 collides with the first bumped alias, from the other declaration form
// the package block takes.
func __gm1() {}
